# mug_table_100 on a link of 80 ms jitter: the host plays each flight on a clock that keeps
# moving its delay, and still shows every table pushed no farther than the same throw solo.
scenario mug_table_jitter
scene mug_tables
seed 41
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 80ms loss 1%

p1 grab mug_a as lift_a
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 -2.4 speed 7 as throw_a
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_b as lift_b
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.4 0 speed 9 as throw_b
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_c as lift_c
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 2 speed 11 as throw_c

expect result lift_a granted
expect result lift_b granted
expect result lift_c granted
expect result throw_c done
# Derived margins, a mode and a table. A table leaves a hit at m v / (m + M) at most (0.3 kg mug, 6 kg
# table) and friction (sqrt(0.6 x 0.3), g 12) stops it over u^2 / (2 mu g): at most 1.1, 1.8 and
# 2.7 cm at 7, 9 and 11 m/s, growing with the square of the hit's speed.
# HOST, a margin a table (test_body_sync_checks --mug-table re-derives them): the host simulates
# the table, struck by its dynamic copy of the mug. Near the host's bodies the copy is driven no
# faster than the thrower's mug as played and coasts, or is taken back, without its correction;
# the velocity grid leaves up to sqrt(3)/64 m/s over her speed: 2 x that / v of the largest slide,
# 0.10, 0.11 and 0.14 mm. The copy plays her clock at fractional ticks, so it meets the table
# anywhere within a tick of where she did and a little off her path: Box3D's answer to the same
# hit over that tick and 1 cm off it passes the solo slide by up to 0.13, 0.04 and 0.88 mm (the
# turning hit). 0.23, 0.15 and 1.02 mm in all. The 1 cm is what these scenes' links showed (7.5 mm
# at most, up to 80 ms of jitter and 5 % loss), not a derived bound: the margins hold for them.
# INTERACTION, 3.4 mm: the thrower takes the table (under the 20 kg light mass) at the hit and
# simulates it with her own mug, solo's physics less what her copy kept of the hit in that step;
# the host's dynamic copy follows her and is left as its world settled it within SYNC_SOFT_HOLD_M
# of her rest pose.
expect moved table_a <= solo 0.03cm interaction 0.34cm
expect moved table_b <= solo 0.02cm interaction 0.34cm
expect moved table_c <= solo 0.11cm interaction 0.34cm
# Every mug hit its table: a travel past the rest hold's 3.4 mm is no rounding of a pose at rest.
# (Under heavy loss a refused take can miss one: a missed effect, README "Contact claims".)
expect moved table_a >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_b >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_c >= 0.34cm
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
